        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-24T17:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Completion of the MMU disable only needs an ISB. The important thing here is to ensure is that whatever we are executing afterwards (fw code as well as payload code) is cleaned from the caches to the point of coherency (PoC) as subsequent instruction fetches won\u0027t hit in unified caches between PoU and PoC.",
      "parentUuid": "6a875065_2c290d65",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "864e5d50_a4d36868",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-25T14:36:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a problem if previous writes have not completed before the MMU and cache are disabled?",
      "parentUuid": "0eb4d543_0fd46195",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
